      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T21:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting - I did not saw it even on Android build which uses LLVM - I wonder how this could be reproduced. I\u0027ve also tried with `make LLVM\u003d1 CC\u003dclang-19` (and some other combinations) and I didn\u0027t encounter any issue with that. AI suggests that it may be reproduicalbe with some older clang version e.g. clang-14 which instead of terminating noreturn function with ` ud2` (as clang-19 does) instead does not terminate with anything (stops generating asembly code) and then objtool reads the binary, follows the control flow to pkvm_get_page(), sees it call pkvm_panic(), and then sees the assembly just stop without a trap.\n\nIf that is the case and this could be only reproducible with some old clang version perhaps it is not worth polluting tools/objtool/noreturns.h. I am not sure, WDYT? @chuanxiao.dong@intel.corp-partner.google.com @dmaluka@google.com?",
